parts.text:
Now the Ollama model list overflow in ProvidersSettingsView (LocalProviderRow). Replace the horizontal ScrollView with a wrapping LazyVGrid.

Current:
```swift
            if !models.isEmpty {
                ScrollView(.horizontal, showsIndicators: false) {
                    HStack(spacing: 6) {
                        ForEach(models, id: \.self) { model in
                            Button(action: { selectModel(model) }) {
                                Text(model)
                                    .interfaceFont(size: 10)
                                    .padding(.horizontal, 8)
                                    .padding(.vertical, 4)
                                    .background(...)
                                    .foregroundColor(...)
                                    .overlay(...)
                                    .clipShape(...)
                            }
                            .buttonStyle(.plain)
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
```

New:
```swift
            if !models.isEmpty {
                LazyVGrid(columns: [GridItem(.adaptive(minimum: 120, maximum: 220), spacing: 6)], alignment: .leading, spacing: 6) {
                    ForEach(models, id: \.self) { model in
                        Button(action: { selectModel(model) }) {
                            Text(model)
                                .interfaceFont(size: 10)
                                .lineLimit(1)
                                .truncationMode(.middle)
                                .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, alignment: .leading)
                                .padding(.horizontal, 8)
                                .padding(.vertical, 4)
                                .background(isSelected(model) ? Color.mimo.brand.opacity(0.2) : Color.mimo.surface)
                                .foregroundColor(isSelected(model) ? Color.mimo.brand : Color.mimo.textSecondary)
                                .overlay(RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 4).stroke(isSelected(model) ? Color.mimo.brand : Color.mimo.border, lineWidth: 1))
                                .clipShape(RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 4))
                        }
                        .buttonStyle(.plain)
                    }
                }
            }
```

Also, the model list could be long (11+ models) → the row grows tall. The card is inside a ScrollView? The ProvidersSettingsView body is a VStack; LocalProvidersSection is in it. Is the whole settings content scrollable? Probably (SettingsView has a ScrollView). To be safe, cap the visible models with a "show all" toggle: show first N (e.g. 12) and a "+N more" button that expands. That prevents the card from becoming enormous. Let me add that: `@State private var showAllModels = false` and display `showAllModels ? models : Array(models.prefix(12))`, plus a button "Show all (N)" / "Show less".

Hmm, the user complained the list "overflows the screen" — a wrapping grid plus a cap solves it.

Let me implement with a cap of 12 and an expand toggle.

Also for long model names (e.g. "fhagenciadigital/ds-go-pro:latest"), the grid cell min width 120 and max 220 with truncation — good.

