Careful: `selectProvider` has side effects (it resolves the model for the provider and persists the "current" values ✓ — that's intended) and it triggers a provider connectivity refresh ✓ (acceptable).

Hmm, but `selectProvider` also sets `defaults.set(providerID, forKey: "com.mycoder.selectedProviderID")` (the current value ✓ fine) and `preferredProviderID` only if persistPreference ✓.

Hmm, one important detail: `selectProvider` internally calls `defaults.set(model, forKey: "com.mycoder.selectedModel")` (the current value) ✓ — fine.

But there's a subtlety: `selectProvider` for the web/auto-free/local providers RESETS selectedModel to that provider's default ✓ — then my subsequent `selectModel(modelID, persistPreference: false)` applies the chat's model ✓ (if available).

Also, the restore must not clobber the global "preferred" values ✓ (persistPreference: false ✓).

